<%# A refresh, not a `replace` of the listing.

    The drawer's POST travels by `fetch` against the FORM's URL, not against the page's:
    `ModalController#_buildURL` only appends `layout=false` to it, so on the other side
    `request.query_parameters` is a bare `{layout=>"false"}`. A listing re-rendered from
    here comes out without the grouping, without the narrowing and without the ordering the
    page had set, and on top of that writes that single param into the toolbar hrefs and into
    ransack's `sort_link`s.

    `turbo_stream.refresh` re-renders nothing here: it asks Turbo to revisit the URL the
    browser already has, which does carry `?group_by=country`. `method: :morph` keeps scroll
    and focus instead of repainting the whole page, and `scroll: :preserve` keeps the position.

    FRAGILITY TO DOCUMENT: Turbo discards a refresh whose `X-Turbo-Request-Id` it has seen
    recently (`isRecentRequest`). The drawer uses bare `fetch`, not `Turbo.fetch`, so it does
    not send that header and the refresh always fires. If ModalController ever moved to
    `Turbo.fetch`, this would stop updating the listing without raising any error. %>
<%= turbo_stream.refresh(method: :morph, scroll: :preserve) %>
